    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "A group G is said to be potent if, to each x ∈ G and each positive integer n\ndividing the order of x (we suppose ∞ is divisible by every positive integer), there\nexists a finite homomorphic image of G in which the image of x has order precisely n.\nIs the free product of two potent groups again potent?            R. B. J. T. Allenby",
